    "knowledge_point": "Finding the Complement of a Set Without a Venn Diagram",
    "problem": "If $U={1,2,3,…,10}$ is the universal set and $A={2,4,6,8,10},$ then the complement of $A$ is",
    "worked_solution": "The complement of $A,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{A},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $A.$\n\nThe elements of $U$ that are not in $A$ are $1,$ $3,$ $5,$ $7,$ and $9.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $A$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{A}={1,3,5,7,9}.\n$$",
